There he is.

30
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.809
Kamran. Raza.

31
00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.768
Did Philippine intelligence track you?

32
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.840
Okay-

33
00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.121
Father.

34
00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.841
Hmm.

35
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.081
You did well.

36
00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.161
Thank you.

37
00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.720
We need to discuss Major General Rahman.

38
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.968
It's your sister's wedding.

39
00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.642
I'm sorry. This can't wait.

40
00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.605
I think your ISI officer was compromised.

41
00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:05.607
Kamran. all Pakistani intelligence officers are compromised.

42
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.889
One of our Afghani friends discovered

43
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.968
a German BND agent in his circle.

44
00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.121
And?

45
00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.169
That particular general won't be very useful to us anymore.

46
00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.730
He's been eliminated.

47
00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.724
Thought you might want to know.

48
00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.404
Don't forget his family.

49
00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.007
Vengeance must always be

50
00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.162
profound and absolute.

51
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.403
So am I. I'm very happy.

52
00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.487
Pentagon just received target confirmation from MI6 ground asset.

53
00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.005
You're clear to execute.

54
00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.882
Hell of a presidential race. sir.

55
00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.529
Every day the same damn joke.

56
00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.286
Seriously?

57
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.840
What the hell did they make you out of?

58
00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.763
Bourbon and poor choices.

59
00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.730
You pick a name yet?

60
00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.167
We were thinking Benjamin if it was a boy.

61
00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.366
Really?

62
00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.521
Hell no!

63
00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:09.130
If it's a girl. maybe.

64
00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:16.881
Voight.

65
00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:19.925
you wanna run over him for me?

66
00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.522
Believe me. sir. we've tried.

67
00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.606
Baby?

68
00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.245
Babe.

69
00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:41.921
Mmm.

70
00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.081
What?

71
00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.684
Little problem in the nursery.

72
00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.604
All right. so six cameras. right?

73
00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.251
One. two. three.

74
00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:00.164
four. five. six.

75
00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.242
What. is that too much? Yeah. maybe.

76
00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.561
Yeah. it's too much. I thought that.

77
00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.165
They're baby gifts from the guys.

78
00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:08.961
I'll take them down.

79
00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.931
All we need is one baby monitor.

80
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.207
One baby monitor. right. okay.

81
00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.208
And a Kevlar mattress.

82
00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.601
Come here.

83
00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.962
Unhand me. Never.

84
00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.566
And guess who just got the next week off?

85
00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.246
Oh. don't toy with me. young man. 'cause there will be consequences.

86
00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.328
No. no. we're finishing this nursery.

87
00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.562
I can't believe it's taken me this long.

88
00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.088
Paint samples. What?

89
00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:45.529
Yeah. Oh. I gotta show you these amazing new paint samples.

90
00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:46.647
Can I get a shower first?

91
00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:47.721
God. yes!

92
00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.247
Sir. Speaker of the House is waiting.

93
00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.244
And the Senate Majority Leader would like five of your time.

94
00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.890
Oh. Um...

95
00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.805
I'll take him first. Hmm.

96
00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:56.846
When is Trumbull getting back?

97
00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.241
The Vice President has three more days of vacation

98
00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:00.924
and insinuated considerable violence

99
00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.610
if he heard my voice before then.

100
00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.729
Yeah. never get between that man and a fish.

101
00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:07.882
Sir. I got your son on video chat.

102
00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.246
Excellent.

103
00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.806
He had his first date last night.

104
00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.804
Mr. President. you need to take this. sir.

105
00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.405
Sir. Speaker of the House?

106
00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.890
You need to take this now. sir.

107
00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.205
This is the President.

108
00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.686
Okay. Thank you.

109
00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.605
Sources confirmed

110
00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:47.001
that Prime Minister James Wilson has died

111
00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.050
while sleeping in his residence at 10 Downing Street.

112
00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.128
He is believed to have suffered a heart attack.

113
00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.602
possibly from complications after a surgical procedure

114
00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.842
to repair his knee a day earlier.

115
00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.764
An autopsy has been scheduled within the next 48 hours

116
00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.649
to determine the actual cause of death.

117
00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:03.721
It's the White House.

118
00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.090
It's okay. My mom can come over.

119
00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.087
What we are proposing

120
00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.089
is that the funeral takes place this Thursday. the 9th.

121
00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.924
4:00 p.m. at St. Paul's.

122
00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.044
The confirmed attendees are all world leaders.

123
00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.691
with the lone exception of the Russian president.

124
00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.364
Well. no love lost there.

125
00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:46.729
Our Royal Family will attend a private service

126
00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.643
at St. James's Palace. the morning of.

127
00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:52.645
with 28 other heads of state from all over the globe.

128
00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:56.327
As per foreign royals. Prince Albert of Monaco.

129
00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.801
Queen Rania of Jordan. Saudi Prince Muqrin.

130
00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.882
Yes. it's a logistical nightmare.

131
00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.764
But let's make sure this runs without a hitch.

132
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.126
Questions?

133
00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.926
And what special requests have the Yank circus demanded so far?

134
00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.010
Dallas Cowboy cheerleaders part of the retinue. possibly?

135
00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:16.367
That's a request I could live with.

136
00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.843
I'm partial to the Kardashians myself. as apparently is Her Majesty.

137
00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.970
Nineteen special requests from 12 different countries.

138
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.082
We've denied all of them.

139
00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.970
Any issues of special concern with our current assessments?

140
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.611
We all know about the 350 or so British nationals

141
00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.922
who've traveled back and forth to Syria in the past year.

142
00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:40.644
as we've seen before in Iraq and Afghanistan.

143
00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.360
Of rising concern is the handful

144
00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:45.805
we believe to be former military.

145
00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.211
Is any of this actionable?

146
00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.850
No.

147
00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.166
Very well.

148
00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.488
Then we will see off our dear friend James with dignity.

149
00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.248
Give him the ceremony he deserves.

150
00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:04.971
Sir?

151
00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.331
Are you ready for us? Oh.

152
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.731
Yeah. come on in.

153
00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.046
Take a seat.

154
00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.968
What are you guys so damn nervous about?

155
00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:23.131
The Brits are world class. We all know their reputation.

156
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.806
But still. these are the trips I hate.

157
00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:29.248
Last minute. Out of the country. No time to plan.

158
00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.448
Are you sure I can't talk you out of this?

159
00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.846
Lynne. it's a state funeral.

160
00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.922
It's our oldest. strongest ally.

161
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.163
I spent half the night on the line with our advance team.

162
00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:43.363
Metropolitan Police will secure the perimeter of the funeral

163
00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.566
at St. Paul's Cathedral.

164
00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.047
Air Force One will land at Stansted Airport.

165
00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.764
On the ground it's all Mike.

166
00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:54.006
Touchdown. Then a 12-minute chopper ride to Somerset House.

167
00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.481
From there we take an armored-vehicle escort

168
00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:59.928
down Fleet Street to the cathedral.

169
00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.205
You don't seem thrilled.

170
00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.209
Well. the British have their hands full.

171
00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:08.489
It's a clusterfuck... Sir.

172
00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.649
Well. 40 different countries

173
00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.404
with 40 different security teams.

174
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.082
Minimal flexibility on approach routes.

175
00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.561
funeral seating. egress.

176
00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.041
Can we make it work?

177
00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.201
Mike?

178
00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.600
I always do. sir.

179
00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:26.921
Good.

180
00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.446
I know it's not great timing for you. but...

181
00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.531
It's what I do.

182
00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:33.931
Thank you. sir.

183
00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.206
There's my man.

184
00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.523
Mr. Vice President. How was your vacation. sir?

185
00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:58.527
Son. do you have any idea the joy a man feels

186
00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.409
pulling a 70-pound king mackerel

187
00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.209
out of the waters around Jekyll Island?

188
00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.606
No. sir. I don't.

189
00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:04.920
That makes two of us.

190
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.401
And I'll have to wait until next year to find out.

191
00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:10.041
But thanks for asking.

192
00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.044
Oh. yeah. that's in the Sinai.

193
00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:26.169
- It's beautiful.
- There you go.

194
00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:28.328
Oh. gee. that's incredible. I love these things. They all are...

195
00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.081
Don't worry about a thing. We'll be fine.

196
00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:38.931
Doris. can we have a minute?

197
00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.485
Sure.

198
00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.485
Oh. you meant Leah. Right.

199
00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:45.686
Very funny. Doris.

200
00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.841
And she tells me not to worry.

201
00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.645
It's only three days.

202
00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.647
Yeah. And I'm not due for two weeks.

203
00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:03.046
The walking away ain't quite so easy this time.

204
00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:07.006
Hey. I got this.

205
00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.321
You go and you do what you have to do

206
00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:14.162
and we will be right here when you get back. okay?

207
00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.244
You. say bye-bye to Daddy.

208
00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:18.961
Hmm.

209
00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.084
Bye-bye. Daddy.

210
00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.361
Bell tolls.

211
00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.481
Yeah.

212
00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.523
I love you.

213
00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.444
You better.

214
00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.250
Behave.

215
00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.161
Uh. here you go. Thank you.

216
00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:10.529
You've been hiding lately. You busy nesting?

217
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:12.682
Something like that. Mmm-hmm.

218
00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:16.481
Your idea of nesting being bullet-proofing the walls of the nursery?

219
00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:18.887
Now. that is actually a great idea.

220
00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.731
Yes.

221
00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:28.650
I'll do it.

222
00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:34.162
Well... That only took two weeks.

223
00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:37.927
Uh-uh. It's no small thing being a godmother.

224
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.606
I mean. I didn't take your asking lightly.

225
00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.321
Oh. I know.

226
00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:45.448
You think you can handle it?

227
00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:47.840
Well. I'm competent. brilliant.

228
00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:50.366
stunningly beautiful and really fucking honored.

229
00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:54.251
Really honored.

230
00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:56.281
Thank you. Lynne.

231
00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.566
Big day ahead.

232
00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.125
Correction. Mega day.

233
00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:18.765
Morning.

234
00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.087
Thank you.

235
00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:26.760
Just your signature here. please. Thank you. sir.

236
00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.811
Gentlemen. ladies.

237
00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.566
Today. I need your undivided best.

238
00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:39.849
The most important people in the world are in our care.

239
00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:42.810
so muck in and get it right.

240
00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:44.484
Always. Chief. Hmm.

241
00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.481
Good morning. London.

242
00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.523
South paw has landed.

243
00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:18.447
Agent Banning. John Lancaster from 5.

244
00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.204
Hey. John. Bit early. aren't you?

245
00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.362
Nope. We're moving up our schedule.

246
00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:23.720
I see.

247
00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:26.844
The fewer people know the President's exact movements. the better.

248
00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.331
Why wasn't I told?

249
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.731
Nobody was.

250
00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:31.529
That's how you keep it a surprise.

251
00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:33.805
Well. thanks for the help.

252
00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.248
With security at unprecedented levels

253
00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:45.288
in anticipation of the funeral.

254
00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.011
set to begin just an hour from now.

255
00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:51.448
this isn't just a gathering of the world's most powerful leaders.

256
00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:54.410
it is the most protected event on Earth.

257
00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:03.728
Rooftops in position.

258
00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.531
All units in position.

259
00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:11.609
Marine One. Two and Three on final approach to Somerset House.

260
00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:14.244
Marine One cleared for landing.

261
00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:33.768
Platoon halt!

262
00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:36.648
Present arms!

263
00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.481
Nein. it's okay.

264
00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:42.965
Arms!

265
00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.245
Thank you.

266
00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.605
Stand at ease!

267
00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.725
Yeah. I understand.

268
00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:02.444
Yeah. I promise.

269
00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:04.522
Everything is going to be fine.

270
00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:07.210
Important matters of state?

271
00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:10.124
That was daughter number two.

272
00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.645
She didn't pass her driving test.

273
